{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4697",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufa4 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) or (quinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 or Ndufv3, which are subunits of the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, and that this binding leads to participation in the activity of the complex, which in turn is associated with Ndufa4. This indicates a potential mechanism by which Metformin may influence Ndufa4's function, possibly through modulation of the Nadh Dehydrogenase activity. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The mechanism appears to involve a common pathway, but the precise role of Ndufa4 in this process and its downstream effects are not yet fully understood.",
